<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Lets a prayer-time notification break through Focus and Do Not Disturb —
		the «عاجلة» badge on the lock screen.

		Claimed for the prayer channel alone (see `_urgencyOf` in
		`lib/core/notifications.dart`). A prayer time is the one thing this app
		sends that is worthless a few minutes late; an adhkar reminder is not,
		and a reader who silenced their phone on purpose should not be
		interrupted for one.

		Without this entitlement iOS quietly downgrades the level to `active`:
		the notification still arrives, it simply respects Focus. So a build that
		has not yet been signed with it is degraded, never broken.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.usernotifications.time-sensitive</key>
	<true/>

	<!--
		Push Notifications. Without it iOS never issues an APNs token, so FCM has
		nothing to map a registration token to and every broadcast and fixed-time
		reminder is dropped on the floor. "development" is correct in the source
		file: Xcode rewrites it to "production" when the archive is exported for
		the App Store.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
